  "stemBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Given that f(x) = (2x + 1)/3 and g(x) = 4x + 5, determine the values of: (i) fg(2) and (ii) f⁻¹(3)."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Think first: One part runs the functions forwards and the other runs f backwards."
    },
    {
      "type": "asset",
      "storagePath": "assets/question_visuals/p146_q09.jpg",
      "altText": "Source visual for edmar-csec-p146-q09 from workbook page 146."
    }
  ],
  "solutionSteps": [
    {
      "stepNo": 1,
      "instruction": "Evaluate g(2).",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "g(2) = 4(2) + 5 = 8 + 5"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: g(2) = 13"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 2,
      "instruction": "Substitute into f.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "f(13) = (2(13) + 1)/3 = 27/3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: fg(2) = 9"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 3,
      "instruction": "Find f⁻¹ by making x the subject of y = (2x + 1)/3.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "3y = 2x + 1 → 2x = 3y − 1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: f⁻¹(x) = (3x − 1)/2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 4,
      "instruction": "Substitute x = 3 into the inverse.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "(3(3) − 1)/2 = 8/2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: f⁻¹(3) = 4"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 5,
      "instruction": "Check the inverse value.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "f(4) = (2(4) + 1)/3 = 9/3 = 3 ✓"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: Confirmed"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "strategyBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Evaluate g(2) and feed it into f for part (i); for part (ii) solve (2x + 1)/3 = 3, or derive f⁻¹ and substitute."
    }
  ],
  "finalAnswerBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "(i) fg(2) = 9  (ii) f⁻¹(3) = 4."
    }
  ],
  "whyThisWorks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "The inverse answers the question 'which input does f send to 3?', so it is found by undoing each operation in reverse order: f multiplies by 2, adds 1 and divides by 3, so f⁻¹ multiplies by 3, subtracts 1 and divides by 2. Because the inverse undoes f exactly, substituting the answer back into f is a complete check."
    }
  ],
